From a502fe264f5f482ba60e13a0679deee6a9c3047b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:36:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: rockchip: rkisp2: Set the CSM range from the pad

The colour space matrix converts RGB to YCbCr with the coefficients the
CSM parameters block carries, but the ISP also has the CSM_Y_FULL_ENA
and CSM_C_FULL_ENA control bits that switch the block from the limited
to the full output range, and the parameters block has no field for the
range. With the bits clear the full range coefficients produce a limited
range picture.

Set the bits when the main path source pad is configured for the full
quantization range, as the vendor driver does, so that the range follows
the colour space negotiated on the pad.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
 drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkisp2/rkisp2-isp.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkisp2/rkisp2-isp.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkisp2/rkisp2-isp.c
@@ -120,6 +120,11 @@ static int rkisp2_config_isp(struct rkis
 				     SW_DEBAYER_FILTER_C_EN);
 
 			isp_ctrl = RKISP2_CIF_ISP_CTRL_ISP_MODE_BAYER_ITU601;
+			if (mp_src_frm->quantization ==
+			    V4L2_QUANTIZATION_FULL_RANGE)
+				isp_ctrl |=
+					RKISP2_CIF_ISP_CTRL_ISP_CSM_Y_FULL_ENA |
+					RKISP2_CIF_ISP_CTRL_ISP_CSM_C_FULL_ENA;
 		}
 	} else if (sink_fmt->pixel_enc == V4L2_PIXEL_ENC_YUV) {
 		acq_mult = 2;
